{'query': 'reputable peer-reviewed scientific source on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'A review of the global climate change impacts, adaptation ...', 'url': 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8978769/', 'snippet': 'This review aims to highlight the effects of climate change in a socio-scientific aspect by analyzing the existing literature on various sectorial pieces of evidence globally that influence the environment.'}, {'title': '(PDF) Understanding Climate Change: A Review of Causes ...', 'url': 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397706496_Understanding_Climate_Change_A_Review_of_Causes_Impacts_and_Responses', 'snippet': 'Nov 18, 2025 · This brief summarizes and analyzes the natural and human causes of the greenhouse effect, the existing scientific evidence, and the environmental, economic, and social impacts of climate...'}, {'title': 'Climate change and its environmental and health effects from ...', 'url': 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405844025006954', 'snippet': 'Feb 15, 2025 · This review seeks to investigate the far-reaching effects of climate change on health and the associated environmental consequences, both on a global scale and within the EMRO region.'}, {'title': 'Science of climate change', 'url': 'https://scienceofclimatechange.org/', 'snippet': 'Science of Climate Change (SCC) is an independent, peer-reviewed, open-access scholarly journal dedicated to advancing scientific understanding of the Earth’s climate system and its governing processes.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change - Recent articles and discoveries - Springer', 'url': 'https://link.springer.com/subjects/climate-change', 'snippet': '1 day ago · Uncover the latest and most impactful research in Climate Change. Explore pioneering discoveries, insightful ideas and new methods from leading researchers in the field.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 4.72883379997802}
{'query': 'government or international body report on climate change causes and effects', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate Reports | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/climatechange/reports', 'snippet': 'The report on Impacts, Adaptation and Vulnerability warns that climate change is causing dangerous disruption in nature and is affecting billions of people, stressing the urgency to act.'}, {'title': 'Causes of Climate Change | US EPA', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/climatechange-science/causes-climate-change', 'snippet': 'Burning fossil fuels changes the climate more than any other human activity.Causes of Climate Change. Natural processes are always influencing the earth’s climate and can explain climate changes prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 1700s.'}, {'title': 'NASA is a global leader in studying Earth’s changing climate.', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'The effects of human-caused global warming are happening now, are irreversible for people alive today, and will worsen as long as humans add greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.Climate change in recent history. Global Ice Viewer. Climate change’s impact on ice.'}, {'title': 'Climate change - Greenpeace UK', 'url': 'https://www.greenpeace.org.uk/challenges/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'The causes and effects of climate change.The UK government could support farmers to move away from these chemicals, but they’re failing to act. Add your name and demand they stand up to the chemical industry. Sign the petition.'}, {'title': 'Climate change', 'url': 'https://www.who.int/health-topics/climate-change', 'snippet': 'Between 2030 and 2050, climate change is expected to cause approximately 250 000 additional deaths per year from malnutrition, malaria, diarrhoea and heat stress alone.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 9.50572829999146}
{'query': 'global average temperatures trend 2023 2024 latest data', 'results': [{'title': 'Global Temperature - Earth Indicator - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/earth/explore/earth-indicators/global-temperature/', 'snippet': 'Jan 21, 2026 · Global temperatures in 2025 were cooler than 2024, with average temperatures of 2.14 degrees Fahrenheit (1.19 degrees Celsius) above the 1951 to 1980 average. The data shown are the latest available, updated annually.'}, {'title': 'NASA Releases Global Temperature Data', 'url': 'https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasa-releases-global-temperature-data/', 'snippet': 'Jan 14, 2026 · Earth’s global surface temperature in 2025 was slightly warmer than 2023 – but within the margin of error: the two years are effectively tied according to an analysis by NASA scientists. Since record-keeping began in 1880, the hottest year on record remains 2024.'}, {'title': 'NASA SVS | Record Temperature Years: 2025, 2024, and 2023', 'url': 'https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5607', 'snippet': 'Feb 4, 2026 · A visualization of global temperature anomalies highlighting the record years of 2025, 2024, and 2023. The visualizations morphs between a data grid showing monthly temperatures and a bar chart of annual temperatures.'}, {'title': 'Global Climate Highlights 2024 | Copernicus', 'url': 'https://climate.copernicus.eu/global-climate-highlights-2024', 'snippet': 'Jan 10, 2025 · 2024 was the warmest year in a multi-dataset record of global temperature going back to 1850. 2024 had a global average temperature of 15.10°C; 0.12°C higher than the previous highest annual value in 2023.'}, {'title': 'Annual 2024 Global Climate Report – Climate Institute', 'url': 'https://climate.org/report/annual-2024-global-climate-report/', 'snippet': 'In total there were 14 straight months of record-breaking global temperatures from June 2023 through July 2024. The July global temperature value was likely the warmest of all months on record.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 6.158817300020019}
